<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33631" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλευσίνιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of Eleusis,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Cer.
				266
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.57
			</span></i>, etc.; epith. of Zeus in Ionia, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; of Artemis in Sicily and Antioch, Id., <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Or.</u>
				11.109
			</span></i>; but mostly of Demeter, <i><span class="en">
				Antim.
				63
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δηὼ Ἐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1120
			</span></i>(lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλευσείνιαι</span> (sic)
				<i>Demeter and Cora,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				4.955.14
			</span></i>(Epid.): hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλευσίνιον, τό</span>, <i>their temple at Eleusis</i>, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.110
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.6.129
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλευσίνια, τά</span>, <i>their festivals</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				12.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				22.847.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				112
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				4.33.5
			</span></i>, etc.: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀττικοὶ τὰ
			Ἐ</span>., of groups of persons confabulating, <i><span class="en">
				Duris
				95
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>: 
				Lacon.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλευηύνια, τά</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(1).213.11
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(v B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλευσίνιος, ὁ</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήν</span>), name of month in Crete, <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				5183
			</span></i>: also spelt 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐλευσύνιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					712.8
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Olus</span>), and so in Thera, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Test.Epict.</u>
				2.7
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				3.3
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῑ</span>, exc. in
				<u>h.Cer.</u>l.c., <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1120
			</span></i>(lyr.).]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
